  "representation": "The existing memory-load table preserves the first 15 tags and appends 12 splat/widen/zero loads. Checked scalar-width byte reads feed existing SIMD splat and low-extension operators; zero loads project raw bytes into zeroed V128 bits. One lane-access table maps 8 guest operators to existing scalar load/store selectors and SIMD replace/extract operators. Lowering reserves consumed address/vector registers before loading resource bindings or temporaries. Lane loads compose checked scalar loads with lane replacement; lane stores extract raw scalar bits then use the existing checked store. Memory32/64, offsets, resource identities, byte ranges, stores and trap effects retain their current authorities. No cell, opcode, selector reinterpretation, executor or residual format added.",
